 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a growing pause between them: 2, 4, 6 and
+8 seconds. The pauses, `BACKOFF_SECONDS` times the attempt number, are set in `larder/capture.py`.
+
+Captures used to stop at 3 attempts sent back to back. The gateway is slow every Friday from 17:00 to 19:00, its
+peak, so all three landed in the same slow minute: one Friday 58 pantry orders were confirmed but never charged, and a
+payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next morning. Replaying that Friday's
+timeouts against the gateway's sandbox, 5 attempts with these pauses would have captured 57 of the 58.
 
 Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
 can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
 drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
+## Known limits
+
+- A capture that keeps timing out holds the member on the confirmation page up to 20 seconds longer than before, the
+  sum of the pauses. The team judged that wait better than volunteers capturing orders by hand.
+- Retries do not outlast a long gateway slowdown: a pantry order whose 5 attempts all time out stays uncharged.
+  Workaround: follow [the gateway-timeouts runbook](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md), and capture the order from the
+  gateway's dashboard.
+
